{
  "version": 4,
  "targetPackage": "com.instagram.android",
  "_comment": "v3, built from a second real dump. Two hard-won rules. (1) Resource IDs match EXACTLY on the short name by default; substring matching made 'main_feed' match 'main_feed_action_bar', which is on every screen. (2) Instagram PRELOADS the Reels tab inside a swipeable ViewPager, so clips_* IDs exist in the tree on every screen including the home feed. Presence proves nothing. Use \"mode\":\"visible\" to require the node actually be on screen. Modes: equals (default), visible, prefix, visiblePrefix, contains.",
  "_chrome_note": "Confirmed present on ALL screens and therefore useless as signals: main_feed_action_bar, tab_bar, clips_tab, feed_tab, direct_tab, search_tab, profile_tab, avatar_container, clips_video_container, clips_viewer_container, clips_viewer_view_pager, clips_media_component, root_clips_layout, container, wrapper, refreshable_container.",
  "screens": {
    "REELS_CREATE": {
      "any": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "contains": "clips_capture"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "contains": "camera_shutter"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "contains": "gallery_picker"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "contains": "media_picker"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "prefix",
          "contains": "creation_"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "contains": "caption_input"
        },
        {
          "type": "contentDesc",
          "contains": "shutter"
        }
      ],
      "none": []
    },
    "REELS_CONSUME": {
      "_comment": "The Reels tab. clips_* IDs are preloaded on every screen, so every matcher here requires the node to be VISIBLE. reel_viewer_* is the STORY viewer in Instagram's legacy naming and must never appear here.",
      "any": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "clips_viewer_view_pager"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "clips_viewer_container"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "clips_video_container"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "clips_ufi_component"
        }
      ],
      "none": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "reel_viewer_root"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visiblePrefix",
          "contains": "row_feed_"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "main_feed_action_bar"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "clips_capture"
        }
      ]
    },
    "REELS_FROM_DM": {
      "_comment": "Provenance (recently in DMs) is the primary signal; these confirm it.",
      "any": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "direct_reply"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "message_composer_container"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "direct_visual_reply"
        }
      ],
      "none": []
    },
    "EXPLORE_GRID": {
      "_comment": "STILL UNCONFIRMED: the capture never reached Explore. Narrow on purpose so it fails open rather than gating the wrong screen. cf_hub_recycler_view is a candidate seen in chrome but unverified, so it is NOT used.",
      "any": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "explore_grid"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "discover_grid"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "explore_recycler"
        }
      ],
      "none": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visiblePrefix",
          "contains": "row_feed_"
        }
      ]
    },
    "SEARCH": {
      "any": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "row_search_user"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "search_result"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "search_row"
        }
      ],
      "none": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "explore_grid"
        }
      ]
    },
    "DMS": {
      "_comment": "CONFIRMED. Inbox: direct_inbox_action_bar / cf_hub_recycler_view. Thread: message_thread_container / thread_view_root / message_list. The old rule used 'direct_thread' with EXACT matching, but no such id exists; the real ones are direct_thread_header and direct_thread_content_below_action_bar, so open threads fell through as UNKNOWN and stopped feeding the sent-reel provenance signal.",
      "any": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "message_thread_container"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "thread_view_root"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "message_list"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "direct_thread_header"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "direct_inbox_action_bar"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "inbox_refreshable_thread_list_recyclerview"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visiblePrefix",
          "contains": "row_thread_composer"
        }
      ],
      "none": []
    },
    "PROFILE": {
      "any": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "profile_header"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "user_detail"
        }
      ],
      "none": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visiblePrefix",
          "contains": "row_feed_"
        }
      ]
    },
    "STORY": {
      "_comment": "CONFIRMED. reel_viewer_root is the story viewer. Checked before REELS_CONSUME.",
      "any": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "reel_viewer_root"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "reel_viewer_media_container"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "reel_viewer_progress_bar"
        }
      ],
      "none": []
    },
    "FEED": {
      "_comment": "CONFIRMED. row_feed_* visible on screen is the home feed. main_feed_action_bar exists everywhere so it may only be used as a VISIBLE check, never presence.",
      "any": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visiblePrefix",
          "contains": "row_feed_"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "reels_tray_container"
        },
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "row_feed_profile_header"
        }
      ],
      "none": [
        {
          "type": "resourceId",
          "mode": "visible",
          "contains": "reel_viewer_root"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "markers": {
    "feedEnd": [
      "suggested for you",
      "suggested posts",
      "you're all caught up",
      "you are all caught up",
      "based on your activity"
    ]
  },
  "storyTray": {
    "_comment": "DISABLED at your request. Ring masking is off; avatar_container turned out to be present on every screen, so the grey donuts stuck everywhere.",
    "containerIds": [],
    "itemIds": []
  },
  "policy": {
    "feedCap": 20,
    "sessionMinutes": 5,
    "gateWordCount": 30,
    "gateMinDistinctWords": 14,
    "gateSimilarityRejectThreshold": 0.65,
    "maskRings": false,
    "ringThicknessFraction": 0.055,
    "ringOuterFraction": 0.92,
    "ringVerticalBiasFraction": 0.44,
    "ringColor": "#FF6E6E6E",
    "dailySessionLimit": 4,
    "dmReelProvenanceMs": 45000,
    "dmReelBounce": true
  },
  "cover": {
    "_comment": "Opaque black boxes drawn over the bounds of these ids whenever they are VISIBLE, independent of screen classification. INTENTIONALLY EMPTY: the Explore grid has never appeared in a capture, so its id is unknown. Do NOT guess with cf_hub_recycler_view - that one is confirmed VISIBLE on the DM inbox and would black out your messages.",
    "enabled": true,
    "ids": []
  }
}